Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?HTDESIGNER-38:=20DFM=20=E4=BD=8D=E7=BD=AE=20--?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20purple=20dashed=20frames=20where=20the=20.dfm=20puts=20each?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20moved=20control;=20a=20drag=20snaps=20onto=20it=20(0.38.0)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

For the BCB6 -> web port: on the design surface, every control whose position
or size differs from its .dfm gets a purple dashed frame at the DFM place.
- the values are in the control's own coordinates (the wrapper shift already
  taken off), only the sides that differ; so the frame stays at the DFM place
  while the control moves, and a drag near it snaps onto it (its edges and
  centre join the snaplines) -- drop it there and it equals the DFM
- the selected control's frame is thicker, labelled "DFM left / top / W×H"
- on / off: right-click menu, command palette, and a button on the DFM
  difference list (which then says on / off); the status bar says DFM 位置;
  while on it is compared again shortly after every edit / re-draw, and the
  difference list's own comparison updates it without a second look
- lib/dfmdiff.ghostsOf(rows): the frames from the difference rows

README: the "no reset-all" line now says only single differences lack it.

Tests: lib (ghostsOf), probe (frame 30px right drawn exactly there with the
label, a 28px drag snaps to +30, off = gone), smoke (spbSave at 64 -> frame
at the DFM 54; the list's button off / on), panels_render (the button),
real VS Code (Setup.Speed: 4 frames for 8 position differences, drawn by the
real probe, off = none, page untouched).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
